 "notes": "CardDemo's Db2 transaction-type list (transaction CTLI, program COTRTLIC, admin menu option 5) on rows generated from the corpus DDL instead of the hand-written seed of carddemo-cotrtlic: 14 CARDDEMO.TRANSACTION_TYPE rows and 20 TRANSACTION_TYPE_CATEGORY rows (equivalence_db2.generate_rows: boundary values, NULLs, unique keys, every category row naming a generated parent type), both compared after each scenario. Scenarios: five stated (the menu entry, no COMMAREA, PF2, PF3, an invalid key), two PF10 ones whose COMMAREA is the confirmation state a previous screen left (DELETE of the generated type ZZ, which no category row names; UPDATE of its description), and 24 generated ones (ENTER / PF8 / PF7 / PF3 / PF5 with a type filter, a description filter and a D / U / S selection typed, first-page COMMAREA). Six generated scenarios (generated-03, -04, -10, -15, -21, -22) reach COTRTLIC's WS-STRING-OUT reference modification with length 0 (a blank info message) and are named in bounds_refused (register X8) as in carddemo-cotrtlic: the harness refuses them rather than compare storage-layout bytes. Not covered, as in carddemo-cotrtlic: 9999-FORMAT-DB2-MESSAGE, which CALLs Db2's DSNTIAC (not modelled) -- a delete refused by the category foreign key (-532), an update or delete of a row gone meanwhile (+100), cursor errors; the stated cases of the hand-seeded case that paged through its seven-type pages and the PF7 backward cursor are not repeated here. Derived from CardDemo (Apache-2.0; Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates): LICENSE here is the source's own, NOTICE names the source and what was written for this case."
